From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Koval <kovalidis@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 01:18:03 +0200
Subject: Restore Ethernet MAC before networking, drop extra DHCP clients

S60netdevice restored the saved eth0/eth1 MAC after S40network had
already started DHCP, and ran its own udhcpc with the stock script next
to the ifup one, adding a default route to the main table and rewriting
resolv.conf. Move the MAC restore into S39macaddr, before networking,
and leave DHCP to ifup. S60netdevice keeps only the USB gadget setup.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
